SlopWorld on Debian 13+ and Ubuntu 26.10+
=======================================

SlopWorld requires tmux 3.7 or newer for emoji widths and terminal state
recovery. Debian 13 ships tmux 3.5a: enable trixie-backports and install
tmux/trixie-backports. Debian testing (forky), unstable (sid), and Ubuntu 26.10
provide a sufficiently recent tmux in their normal repositories. The package
is built against Debian 13 libraries; APT checks its runtime dependencies.
For distribution-specific commands, see:
https://slopworld.space/installation/linux.html
Rebuilding SlopWorld does not remove the tmux requirement.

The package stages the mod at /usr/share/slopworld/SlopWorld. As your normal
user, attach it to a separately installed native Linux RimWorld 1.6 game:

  RIMWORLD=/path/to/RimWorld/game
  slopworld mod install --game "$RIMWORLD"
  systemctl --user daemon-reload
  systemctl --user enable --now slopd.service
  slopworld

The installer saves the game directory as the launcher default. The source defaults to
`/usr/share/slopworld/SlopWorld`; use `--source DIR` for another mod tree.
You can omit --game when RIMWORLD is exported or the game path is already saved.
Enable SlopWorld in the launched game's mod list. After package upgrades, refresh
the mod, reload the user unit, and restart the daemon as your normal user:

  slopworld mod install

  systemctl --user daemon-reload
  systemctl --user try-restart slopd.service

Before removal, stop and disable the daemon as your normal user:

  systemctl --user disable --now slopd.service
  slopworld mod uninstall

After package removal, run systemctl --user daemon-reload.
The package leaves per-user configuration, sessions, and game saves intact.
A user unit under ~/.config/systemd/user takes precedence over the packaged
unit; remove a previous source installation's unit before enabling this one.

File paging and highlighting use the required bat and less packages. Bat renders
files and less provides interactive paging. Auto selection and custom commands
remain available.

The required xclip package provides clipboard and PRIMARY selection on the game's
X11/XWayland desktop, including connections to remote daemons.

Optional integrations
---------------------

The Suggests field lists optional packages; install those for the features you use.

  highlight             Alternative syntax highlighter.
  python3-pygments      Alternative highlighter (pygmentize).
  libglib2.0-bin        Desktop associations and launching (gio), portal access (gdbus).
  python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-3.0
                        Full native Open With chooser, using Python and GTK 3.
  xdg-desktop-portal    Open With fallback; also requires a backend appropriate
                        to your desktop and OpenURI interface version 3 or newer.
  xsel                  Fallback to the required xclip tool.
  procps                Fallback process inspection.

Debian names the bat executable batcat; SlopWorld Auto and the bat selector
resolve the installed executable automatically.

Spotify playback requires ncspot and Spotify Premium; song recognition requires
songrec. These are not provided by the official target distribution repositories;
install them separately if needed. The game must find songrec on its PATH, and
the daemon must find ncspot on its PATH.
